=product @PRODUCER@ @BASE@ VMSMARIADB @PCSIVERSION@ full
1 'PRODUCER
=prompt @PRODUCER@
1 'PRODUCT
=prompt MariaDB @VERSION@ for OpenVMS x86-64 (vms-mariadb, preview)
1 'NOTICE
=prompt MariaDB is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2.
1 RELEASE_NOTES
=prompt Documentation is in [VMSMARIADB.DOC]README.VMS under the installation directory.
1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for MariaDB (vms-mariadb)
    At system startup: to define VMSMARIADB$ROOT at every boot, add this
    line to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSMARIADB$STARTUP.COM
    For each user: to define the mariadb commands, add this line to
    LOGIN.COM (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone):
    $ @VMSMARIADB$ROOT:[000000]VMSMARIADB$SETUP.COM
    To create a data directory (on an ODS-5 disk) and start a server:
    $ @VMSMARIADB$ROOT:[000000]VMSMARIADB$SERVER INSTALL_DB dev:[dir.DATA]
    $ @VMSMARIADB$ROOT:[000000]VMSMARIADB$SERVER START dev:[dir.DATA]
    The new root@localhost account has no password: set one.

PRODUCT REMOVE VMSMARIADB removes the product and deassigns VMSMARIADB$ROOT;
data directories are not touched.
